{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CesdxmrZoNUfmmpufQC8R","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Repository findings:**\n\n- Shipment model: `sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/shipment/Shipment.kt:9` — has three statuses (CREATED, CONFIRMED, CANCELLED)\n- ShipmentController: `sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/shipment/ShipmentController.kt:20` — currently has create, getById, list; no confirm endpoint\n- ShipmentRepository: `sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/shipment/ShipmentRepository.kt:10` — in-memory store with save/findById/findAll\n- ApiExceptions: `sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/api/ApiExceptions.kt:19-24` — ResourceNotFoundException (404) and ConflictException (409)\n- ErrorCode enum: `sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/api/ApiError.kt:31` — includes SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND, SHIPMENT_ALREADY_EXISTS, but no code for invalid state\n- GlobalExceptionHandler: `sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/api/GlobalExceptionHandler.kt:16` — handles ApiException → JSON response\n- Tests: `sample-service/src/test/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/shipment/ShipmentControllerTest.kt:23` — uses MockMvc with jsonPath assertions\n\n**Conventions already in place:**\n\n1. Controllers throw ApiException subclasses (ResourceNotFoundException, ConflictException) which are caught by GlobalExceptionHandler\n2. ErrorCode enum is the machine-readable error identifier in the API contract\n3. Success status codes: CREATED (201) for POST creation, OK (200) for GET\n4. Error responses wrapped in `{ \"error\": { \"code\": \"...\", \"message\": \"...\", \"fields\": [...] } }` envelope\n5. Tests use `@BeforeEach` to reset repository state, MockMvc to make requests, jsonPath to assert responses\n\n**Affected files:**\n\n1. **ShipmentController.kt** — Must add `POST /shipments/{shipmentId}/confirm` endpoint\n2. **ApiError.kt** — Must add new ErrorCode for the \"cannot confirm\" scenario (SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE or similar)\n3. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** — Must add tests covering all four cases: confirm created → confirmed, confirm confirmed → no-op, confirm cancelled → 409, confirm missing → 404\n\n**Risks:**\n\n- Adding a new ErrorCode is part of the public API contract and should be deliberate\n- The idempotent behavior (confirming already-confirmed succeeds) must be distinguished from other state violations\n- Must ensure existing tests still pass\n\n**Open questions:**\n\nNone — the requirement is fully defined.\n\n---\n\n```\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n```\n\n**Proposed changes, file by file:**\n\n1. **ApiError.kt**: Add `SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE` to ErrorCode enum. This code covers the case where a shipment's current state (e.g., CANCELLED) prevents the confirm operation. The ticket defines this as HTTP 409 Conflict.\n\n2. **ShipmentController.kt**: Add a new `@PostMapping(\"/{shipmentId}/confirm\")` method that:\n   - Fetches the shipment by ID; if missing, throw ResourceNotFoundException with SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND (404)\n   - If status is CREATED, update it to CONFIRMED, save, and return the updated shipment (200 OK)\n   - If status is CONFIRMED, return the shipment unchanged (200 OK) — this is the idempotent case\n   - If status is CANCELLED, throw ConflictException with SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE (409)\n\n3. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt**: Add four new test methods:\n   - `confirms a created shipment` — creates S-1 with CREATED, confirms it, checks response is CONFIRMED\n   - `confirm already-confirmed shipment succeeds without change` — creates S-2, confirms twice, second succeeds\n   - `confirms a cancelled shipment with 409` — manually insert a CANCELLED shipment, try to confirm, expect 409 with SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE code\n   - `confirms a missing shipment with 404` — try to confirm non-existent shipment, expect 404 with SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND code\n\n**Alternative considered and rejected:**\n\n- Alternative: Add a service class (ShipmentService) to encapsulate the confirm logic. Rejected because the existing codebase has no service layer — controllers talk directly to repositories — and adding one would be unrelated refactoring beyond the scope of the ticket.\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\n1. **Happy path (CREATED → CONFIRMED)**:\n   - Request: `POST /shipments/S-1/confirm`\n   - Repository.findById(\"S-1\") → Shipment(..., status=CREATED)\n   - Create new Shipment with status=CONFIRMED, same other fields\n   - Repository.save() → updates in-memory store\n   - Response: 200 OK, Shipment JSON with status=CONFIRMED\n\n2. **Idempotent path (CONFIRMED → CONFIRMED)**:\n   - Request: `POST /shipments/S-2/confirm`\n   - Repository.findById(\"S-2\") → Shipment(..., status=CONFIRMED)\n   - No state change, but return the shipment as-is\n   - Response: 200 OK, Shipment JSON with status=CONFIRMED\n\n3. **Conflict path (CANCELLED)**:\n   - Request: `POST /shipments/S-3/confirm`\n   - Repository.findById(\"S-3\") → Shipment(..., status=CANCELLED)\n   - Throw ConflictException(SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE, \"Shipment ... is CANCELLED and cannot be confirmed\")\n   - GlobalExceptionHandler catches it\n   - Response: 409 Conflict, JSON error with code=SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE\n\n4. **Not found path**:\n   - Request: `POST /shipments/missing/confirm`\n   - Repository.findById(\"missing\") → null\n   - Throw ResourceNotFoundException(SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND, \"No shipment with id 'missing'\")\n   - GlobalExceptionHandler catches it\n   - Response: 404 Not Found, JSON error with code=SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND\n\n**Test strategy:**\n\n- Test 1: Confirm created shipment → state changes to CONFIRMED\n- Test 2: Confirm already-confirmed shipment → state remains CONFIRMED, succeeds (idempotent)\n- Test 3: Confirm cancelled shipment → 409 with SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE code\n- Test 4: Confirm missing shipment → 404 with SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND code\n\nAll tests use MockMvc to POST to `/shipments/{id}/confirm`, check status code and jsonPath assertions on the response.\n\n---\n\n```\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n```\n\nNow I'll implement the changes:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":289,"cache_read_input_tokens":16664,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":289},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"34270a19-dff9-47e0-8644-52d833eb245c","uuid":"828240cf-6c22-4748-b8e8-b252a92de023","timestamp":"2026-09-09T09:35:44.234Z","request_id":"req_011Cesdxm9eeSh12M5X6Zoat"}
